  "question": {
    "text": "The ordinates of the points $P$ and $Q$ on the parabola with focus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and directrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;are in the ratio<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the point of intersection of the tangents to the parabola at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Focus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, Directrix, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, the equation of parabola will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Now taking the parametric point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;plotting the diagram we get,<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0030_6521324b64f5.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 298px;\" /><br />Now we know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;will be the aithematic mean of ordinate&nbsp;and geometric mean of abscissa<br />will be,</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>So, putting the value in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>given</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
